== Biochemical mechanism ==
Most bioluminescent systems involve oxidation of a light-emitting substrate commonly called a ''luciferin''. The reaction is typically catalyzed by a ''luciferase'' enzyme or occurs within a photoprotein system. Oxygen is commonly required, while cofactors and reaction details vary among lineages.

There is no single universal luciferin–luciferase system: bioluminescence evolved multiple times and uses chemically distinct mechanisms in different organisms.
